guamp: metal2vulkan runtime patches 0025-0027, the bridge's CPU per frame (agent gpu-bridge, 06/11)

0025: docs/FAST-PATHS.md and tests/fast_paths.rs class PaddedReadsPolicy::AliasWrites, the value 0008 adds; without it the
metal2vulkan lib tests do not compile (E0004 in the ledger's exhaustive match). Test only, no runtime change.
0026: the spare command pools and descriptor pools are reset as their command buffer gives them back (completion thread, inside
a section of the exit guard, vkResetCommandPool/vkResetDescriptorPool added to the guard's table and primed), not by the next
taker on the encoding thread: backboardd's render thread no longer pays the reset of its command buffer's pool and of each
descriptor pool its draws open. A pool whose reset there fails, or one given back while the process exits, stays dirty and its
taker resets it as before. Measured on lavapipe with 0027 (40 draws a frame): encoding thread CPU per frame 1537 -> 1331 us
(4 interleaved pairs). metal2vulkan-runtime lib tests spares/exit_guard/descriptor_arena/prime: 40 passed.
0027: example draw_costs (FRAMES=400 cargo run --release -p metal2vulkan-runtime --example draw_costs): a Core Animation-like
frame loop that prints the D/C/B phases per draw, per close and per commit and the encoding thread's CPU, for host A/B.

